  "strategy": "1. Approach and Rationale\n   Central Idea: We adopt a multi-phase optimization strategy combining grid coarsening, random restarts, and entropy-regularized gradient descent to tackle the non-convex nature of the Erd\u0151s minimum overlap problem. The method first explores a coarse grid (N=8) to escape local minima, then refines solutions at finer grids (N=16, 32, 64) with adaptive hyperparameter scheduling. This approach directly minimizes the smooth entropy version of the overlap integral, allowing escape from scale-dependent local optima while maintaining constraint enforcement through projected gradient steps.\n\n   Key limitations addressed:\n   - Previous methods struggled with the non-differentiable max operation\n   - Fixed resolution optimizations trapped in frequency-dependent minima\n   - Standard local searches failed to explore low-frequency solutions\n\n2. Mathematical Specification\n   Variables: h \u2208 [0,1]^N with \u2211h_i = N/2\n   Objective: Minimize J(h, S) = (1/S) log(sum_k exp(S * dx * h_{i}(1-h_{i+k})))\n   where dx=2.0/N, S=35 (temperature scaling)\n   Constraints: 0\u2264h_i\u22641, \u2211h_i=N/2\n   Uses entropy smoothing to create a differentiable surrogate for the max operation\n\n3. Implementation Procedure\n   Stage 1: Coarse initialization (N=8)\n     - Start from parent solution (N=320) upsampled using cubic interpolation\n     - Binary-coded initialization: randomly set 4 out of 8 points to 0,50 to 1\n     - Trust-region optimizer with automatic temperature reduction\n\n   Stage 2: Progressive refinement (N=16\u219232\u219264)\n     - Smooth projection of feasible solutions using linear interpolation\n     - Coordinate-wise line searches with soft thresholding gradients\n     - Dynamic temperature adjustment based on improvement rate\n\n   Stage 3: Final polishing (N=32\u2192final)\n     - Adams-Bashforth extrapolation from surrogate solutions\n     - Gradient penalty enforcement for integral constraint\n     - Two-pass optimization with adaptive bounds tightening\n\n   Helper functions needed:\n   - constrain_by_integral(h, target=None) [guarantees \u2211h_i = N/2 with box constraints]\n   - entropy_smooth(h, S) [smooth surrogate objective computation]\n   - derivative_estimator(X, h) [analytic gradient calculation for smoothed objective]\n\n4. Search Choices\n   - Base temperature: 35.0 (start value and reduction schedule)\n   - Grid sequence: [8,16,32,64]\n   - Maximum iterations: 800 (decaying by 2/3 per grid level)\n   - Line search tolerance: 0.1 (conservative to maintain constraint satisfaction)\n\n5. Compute Budget\n   - N=8: 80 seconds\n   - N=16: 140 seconds\n   - N=32: 220 seconds\n   - N=64: 310 seconds\n   - Total estimated: 750 seconds\n   - Automatic fallback for time constraints\n\n6. Validation Contract\n   - Returns (h_final, c5_bound, N)\n   - h_final must satisfy: 0\u2264h_i\u22641 and \u2211h_i\u2248N/2 (tolerance 1e-4)\n   - Objectives re-verified at final N\n   - Uses direct correlation for metric: C5 = (max_lag correlation) * dx",
